1a:["$","$L1c",null,{"items":[{"id":"chevening-2027","title":"Chevening Scholarships 2027–2028","provider":"UK Government","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"United Kingdom","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"6 October 2026, 11:00 UTC","deadlineDate":"2026-10-06","deadlineAt":"2026-10-06T11:00:00Z","status":"Closed","summary":"The 2027–2028 scholarship application round is closed. Existing applicants should follow the official assessment, interview and later university-offer instructions.","tags":["Leadership","International students","One-year master's"],"source":"https://www.chevening.org/scholarships/","sourceLabel":"Chevening official website","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":false},{"id":"schwarzman-2027","title":"Schwarzman Scholars 2027–2028","provider":"Schwarzman Scholars","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"China","region":"Asia","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"9 September 2026, 3:00 p.m. EDT","deadlineDate":"2026-09-09","status":"Closed","summary":"The 2027–2028 global application is closed. The next U.S./Global application cycle is expected from April to September 2027.","tags":["Global affairs","Leadership","Tsinghua University"],"source":"https://www.schwarzmanscholars.org/admissions/application-instructions/","sourceLabel":"Schwarzman Scholars official website","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"knight-hennessy-2027","title":"Knight-Hennessy Scholars 2027","provider":"Stanford University","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"United States","region":"North America","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"6 October 2026, 1:00 p.m. PT","deadlineDate":"2026-10-06","deadlineAt":"2026-10-06T13:00:00-07:00","status":"Closed","summary":"The 2027 KHS application is closed. Existing candidates must still follow their separate Stanford degree deadlines; the next KHS cohort is announced to open in summer 2027.","tags":["Stanford","Graduate study","Leadership"],"source":"https://knight-hennessy.stanford.edu/admission","sourceLabel":"Knight-Hennessy official website","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":false},{"id":"rhodes-2027","title":"Rhodes Scholarship 2027","provider":"Rhodes Trust","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"United Kingdom","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"2027-entry round closed; next applications reopen in 2027 for 2028 entry","status":"Closed","summary":"Applications are closed. Prepare by constituency and eligible Oxford course; future-cycle exact dates must come from the next official call.","tags":["Oxford","Postgraduate","Leadership"],"source":"https://www.rhodeshouse.ox.ac.uk/scholarships/the-rhodes-scholarship/","sourceLabel":"Rhodes Trust: current application status","checked":"24 October 2026","featured":false},{"id":"gates-cambridge-2027","title":"Gates Cambridge Scholarship","provider":"University of Cambridge","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"United Kingdom","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"International: 8 Dec 2026 or 6 Jan 2027, course-dependent; U.S. round closed","deadlineDate":"$undefined","milestones":[{"label":"International funding deadline: course-dependent December option","date":"2026-12-08","at":"2026-12-08T23:59:00Z","detail":"Your course determines whether December or January applies; references must be complete."},{"label":"International funding deadline: course-dependent January option","date":"2027-01-06","at":"2027-01-06T23:59:00Z","detail":"Not a second chance after a December deadline. Check your course and Gates route."}],"status":"Check official site","summary":"The U.S. deadline has passed. Other eligible applicants must check the exact course funding deadline and Gates route; a complete application includes references.","tags":["Cambridge","Master's","PhD"],"source":"https://www.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/funding","sourceLabel":"Cambridge: 2027–28 funding deadlines","checked":"24 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"commonwealth-masters-2027","title":"Commonwealth Master's Scholarships 2027–2028","provider":"Commonwealth Scholarship Commission","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"United Kingdom","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"20 October 2026, 16:00 BST","deadlineDate":"2026-10-20","status":"Closed","summary":"The published central 2027–2028 deadline of 20 October 2026 at 16:00 BST has passed. Existing applicants should retain confirmations and follow CSC and nominator instructions; check the official portal for any amendment.","tags":["Commonwealth","Development","Master's"],"source":"https://cscuk.fcdo.gov.uk/scholarships/commonwealth-masters-scholarships/","sourceLabel":"Commonwealth Scholarship Commission","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":false,"deadlineAt":"2026-10-20T16:00:00+01:00"},{"id":"commonwealth-phd-2027","title":"Commonwealth PhD Scholarships 2027–2028","provider":"Commonwealth Scholarship Commission","type":"Scholarship","level":"PhD","country":"United Kingdom","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"20 October 2026, 16:00 BST","deadlineDate":"2026-10-20","status":"Closed","summary":"The published central 2027–2028 deadline of 20 October 2026 at 16:00 BST has passed. Existing applicants should retain confirmations and follow CSC and nominator instructions; check the official portal for any amendment.","tags":["Commonwealth","Research","PhD"],"source":"https://cscuk.fcdo.gov.uk/scholarships/commonwealth-phd-scholarships-for-least-developed-countries-and-vulnerable-states/","sourceLabel":"Commonwealth Scholarship Commission","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":false,"deadlineAt":"2026-10-20T16:00:00+01:00"},{"id":"erasmus-mundus-2027","title":"Erasmus Mundus Joint Masters 2027","provider":"European Union","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"Multiple European countries","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"Consortium-specific; check the current programme call","status":"Check official site","summary":"Joint master's programmes use their own calls and scholarship deadlines. The European Commission describes many applications between October and January, but this umbrella record is not a confirmed open call.","tags":["Europe","Joint degree","Mobility"],"source":"https://erasmus-plus.ec.europa.eu/opportunities/individuals/students/erasmus-mundus-joint-masters","sourceLabel":"European Commission – Erasmus+","checked":"13 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"daad-epos-2027","title":"DAAD EPOS Scholarships 2027–2028","provider":"DAAD","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"Germany","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"Varies by selected postgraduate course","status":"Check official site","summary":"Development-related postgraduate funding for graduates from eligible countries, generally requiring at least two years of professional experience.","tags":["Germany","Development","Professional experience"],"source":"https://www2.daad.de/deutschland/stipendium/datenbank/en/21148-scholarship-database/?detail=50076777","sourceLabel":"DAAD scholarship database","checked":"13 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"mext-2027","title":"Japanese Government MEXT Scholarships","provider":"Government of Japan","type":"Scholarship","level":"Any degree","country":"Japan","region":"Asia","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"Varies by embassy or university route","status":"Check official site","summary":"Japanese government scholarships for international students selected through embassy, university or authority recommendation routes.","tags":["Japan","Embassy route","University route"],"source":"https://www.mext.go.jp/en/policy/education/highered/title02/detail02/sdetail02/1373897.htm","sourceLabel":"MEXT official website","checked":"13 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"fulbright-foreign-student","title":"Fulbright Foreign Student Program","provider":"U.S. Department of State","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"United States","region":"North America","funding":"Funded","deadline":"Varies by home country","status":"Check official site","summary":"Approximately 4,000 annual grants for foreign graduate students, young professionals and artists; local rules vary by country.","tags":["USA","Master's","Research"],"source":"https://foreign.fulbrightonline.org/apply","sourceLabel":"Foreign Fulbright Program","checked":"13 October 2026"},{"id":"stipendium-hungaricum","title":"Stipendium Hungaricum Scholarship","provider":"Government of Hungary","type":"Scholarship","level":"Any degree","country":"Hungary","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"2027–2028 call not confirmed on the official apply page checked 13 October","status":"Check official site","summary":"The official apply page still describes 2026–2027 and its past 15 January 2026 deadline. Prepare by sending-partner route; do not reuse that date for an unannounced future cycle.","tags":["Hungary","Bachelor's","Master's","PhD"],"source":"https://stipendiumhungaricum.hu/apply/","sourceLabel":"Stipendium Hungaricum official website","checked":"13 October 2026"},{"id":"lester-b-pearson-2027","title":"Lester B. Pearson International Scholarship 2027","provider":"University of Toronto","type":"Scholarship","level":"Bachelor's","country":"Canada","region":"North America","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"School nomination: 9 Oct; admission: 16 Oct; scholarship: 6 Nov 2026","deadlineDate":"2026-10-09","milestones":[{"label":"School nomination","date":"2026-10-09","detail":"School acts first; later deadlines do not replace nomination."},{"label":"Undergraduate admission","date":"2026-10-16","detail":"Student follows the University of Toronto route."},{"label":"Scholarship form and documents","date":"2026-11-06","detail":"Nominated student uses the official invitation."}],"status":"Open","summary":"School nomination and the required admission deadline have passed. Applicants who completed both steps can submit their scholarship form and documents by 6 November 2026 through their private university invitation.","tags":["University of Toronto","School nomination","Undergraduate"],"source":"https://future.utoronto.ca/pearson-scholarships","sourceLabel":"University of Toronto official scholarship page","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":true,"entryDeadlineDate":"2026-10-09","entryClosedNote":"School nomination closed on 9 October. Remaining admission and award deadlines apply to already nominated candidates."},{"id":"australia-awards-scholarships","title":"Australia Awards Scholarships","provider":"Australian Government Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade","type":"Scholarship","level":"Any degree","country":"Australia","region":"Oceania","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"Country-specific; check the participating-country profile","status":"Check official site","summary":"Long-term undergraduate and postgraduate awards for eligible developing-country applicants, with benefits generally including tuition, travel, living support and health cover.","tags":["Developing countries","Government scholarship","Return-home condition"],"source":"https://www.dfat.gov.au/people-to-people/australia-awards/australia-awards-scholarships","sourceLabel":"Australian Government DFAT","checked":"13 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"australia-rtp","title":"Australian Government Research Training Program","provider":"Australian Government Department of Education","type":"Scholarship","level":"PhD","country":"Australia","region":"Oceania","funding":"Funded","deadline":"University-specific; apply through an eligible Australian provider","status":"Check official site","summary":"University-administered support for eligible research doctorate and research master's students that may include a tuition-fee offset, stipend and research-related allowances.","tags":["Research degree","University application","Tuition and stipend"],"source":"https://www.education.gov.au/research-block-grants/research-training-program","sourceLabel":"Australian Government Department of Education","checked":"13 October 2026"},{"id":"italy-maeci-2026-27","title":"MAECI Italian Government Grants 2026–2027","provider":"Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","country":"Italy","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"26 March 2026, 14:00 Italian time — closed","deadlineDate":"2026-03-26","status":"Closed","summary":"The current call is closed. MAECI grants use an annual eligible-country list and the official Study in Italy application portal for study carried out in Italy.","tags":["Italian Government","MAECI","Study in Italy"],"source":"https://www.esteri.it/en/servizi-opportunita/opportunita/borse-di-studio/per-cittadini-stranieri/borsestudio_stranieri/","sourceLabel":"Italian Ministry of Foreign Affairs","checked":"13 October 2026"},{"id":"italy-ergo-dsu-2026-27","title":"ER.GO Regional Scholarship 2026–2027","provider":"ER.GO Emilia-Romagna","type":"Scholarship","level":"Any degree","country":"Italy","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"24 August 2026, 16:00 — main scholarship deadline closed","deadlineDate":"2026-08-24","status":"Closed","summary":"Regional right-to-study support assessed under ER.GO's economic, enrolment and merit rules, with separate guidance for families holding income or assets abroad.","tags":["DSU","Emilia-Romagna","Income assessed"],"source":"https://www.er-go.it/cosa-fare-per/bandi-di-concorso/leggi-il-bando","sourceLabel":"ER.GO official 2026–2027 call","checked":"13 October 2026"},{"id":"padua-international-excellence-2026-27","title":"Padua International Excellence Scholarship","provider":"University of Padua","type":"Scholarship","level":"Any degree","country":"Italy","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"2027–2028 award terms: verify on the official scholarship page","status":"Check official site","summary":"The 2026–2027 scheme offered €8,000 gross per year plus a tuition-fee exemption for selected international students in eligible English-taught degrees.","tags":["Padua","Merit","English-taught degree"],"source":"https://www.unipd.it/en/padua-international-excellence-scholarship-programme","sourceLabel":"University of Padua","checked":"13 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"polimi-merit-scholarships-2027-28","title":"Politecnico di Milano International Merit Scholarships","provider":"Politecnico di Milano","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"Italy","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"15 December 2026, noon Italian time; early admission payment required by 1 December","deadlineDate":"2026-12-15","deadlineAt":"2026-12-15T12:00:00+01:00","milestones":[{"label":"Required early admission payment","date":"2026-12-01","detail":"Confirm your eligible early-bird route and closing time."},{"label":"Merit scholarship form","date":"2026-12-15","at":"2026-12-15T12:00:00+01:00","detail":"Noon Italian time; prior admission conditions apply."}],"status":"Open","summary":"The 2027–2028 merit call has a separate form closing 15 December at noon Italian time, after qualifying early admission payment by 1 December. The PDF lists an acceptance administrative fee around €190; check award-specific benefits and English evidence.","tags":["Polimi","Master of Science","Tuition waiver"],"source":"https://www.polimi.it/en/prospective-students/how-much-does-it-cost/scholarships","sourceLabel":"Politecnico di Milano","checked":"23 October 2026","featured":true},{"id":"schwarzman-2028-announced","title":"Schwarzman Scholars 2028–2029 — announced next cycle","provider":"Schwarzman Scholars","type":"Scholarship","level":"Master's","country":"China","region":"Asia","funding":"Fully funded","status":"Opening soon","deadline":"U.S./Global application period: April–September 2027; exact dates to verify","summary":"The official instructions announce the next U.S./Global cycle for April–September 2027, with the programme beginning August 2028. Chinese-citizenship applicants have a different March–May 2027 period. Applications are not open in this record.","tags":["Announced future cycle","Leadership","Different citizenship routes"],"source":"https://www.schwarzmanscholars.org/admissions/application-instructions/","sourceLabel":"Schwarzman official application instructions","checked":"23 October 2026"},{"id":"open-doors-2026","title":"Open Doors: 2026 competition for study in Russia","provider":"Global Universities Association","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","supportedDegrees":["Bachelor's","Master's","PhD"],"country":"Russia","region":"Europe","funding":"Funded","deadline":"Registration: 1 November 2026; confirm account cut-off","deadlineDate":"2026-11-01","status":"Open","summary":"Tuition-free study routes with university-dependent stipend; additional support has separate conditions. Choose the correct academic track and follow the official stages.","tags":["Bachelor’s","Master’s","PhD","Track-specific rules"],"source":"https://od.globaluni.ru/","sourceLabel":"Official Open Doors rules, schedule and FAQ","checked":"24 October 2026"},{"id":"turkiye-next","title":"Türkiye Scholarships: prepare for the next degree call","provider":"Türkiye Scholarships / YTB","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","supportedDegrees":["Bachelor's","Master's","PhD"],"country":"Türkiye","region":"Europe","funding":"Fully funded","deadline":"Annual Jan–Feb calendar; next named call must be verified","status":"Check official site","summary":"Degree funding with placement and level-specific academic/age conditions. The published annual calendar does not confirm that the next intake is open.","tags":["Degree placement","TBBS","Level-specific requirements"],"source":"https://www.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/fulltimeprograms","sourceLabel":"Türkiye Scholarships official full-time programme","checked":"24 October 2026"},{"id":"kfupm-graduate","title":"KFUPM graduate scholarship routes","provider":"King Fahd University of Petroleum and Minerals","type":"Scholarship","level":"Graduate","supportedDegrees":["Master's","PhD"],"country":"Saudi Arabia","region":"Middle East","funding":"Varies","deadline":"Programme and intake-specific; verify current graduate call","status":"Check official site","summary":"Compare thesis MS, project MS and doctoral requirements. Minimum admission eligibility, scholarship selection and self-sponsored fees are separate decisions.","tags":["Thesis / project","Graduate research","Funding conditions"],"source":"https://cgis.kfupm.edu.sa/admission/kfupm-scholarship","sourceLabel":"KFUPM official scholarship terms","checked":"24 October 2026"}],"showTypeFilter":false}]
1b:["$","article",null,{"className":"article-body ","children":[null,["$","section","1-Start with eligibility, not prestige",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-2","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Start with eligibility, not prestige"}],[["$","p","A famous scholarship is useful only when your citizenship, degree level, field, work experience and intended course satisfy the published rules. Build a shortlist in three tiers: strong fit, possible fit and aspirational.",{"children":"A famous scholarship is useful only when your citizenship, degree level, field, work experience and intended course satisfy the published rules. Build a shortlist in three tiers: strong fit, possible fit and aspirational."}],["$","p","For every shortlisted award, record its funding scope. Fully funded can still exclude dependants, visa charges, tests or some travel costs.",{"children":"For every shortlisted award, record its funding scope. Fully funded can still exclude dependants, visa charges, tests or some travel costs."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined",["$","ul",null,{"children":[["$","li","Confirm nationality and residency rules",{"children":"Confirm nationality and residency rules"}],["$","li","Check degree and graduation-date requirements",{"children":"Check degree and graduation-date requirements"}],["$","li","Identify required work or leadership experience",{"children":"Identify required work or leadership experience"}],["$","li","Verify whether university admission is separate",{"children":"Verify whether university admission is separate"}],["$","li","Calculate costs not covered by the award",{"children":"Calculate costs not covered by the award"}]]}],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],["$","section","2-Build a scholarship portfolio, not one risky bet",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Build a scholarship portfolio, not one risky bet"}],[["$","p","Divide your shortlist into opportunities with different selection models. A government leadership scholarship, a university merit award and a research assistantship may judge different strengths. This reduces dependence on one result and helps you reuse verified evidence without sending identical applications.",{"children":"Divide your shortlist into opportunities with different selection models. A government leadership scholarship, a university merit award and a research assistantship may judge different strengths. This reduces dependence on one result and helps you reuse verified evidence without sending identical applications."}],["$","p","Record the official owner, intake, application route, funding exclusions and decision schedule for every programme. Remove an opportunity when a mandatory rule fails; time spent improving a strong-fit application is more valuable than trying to argue around an eligibility condition.",{"children":"Record the official owner, intake, application route, funding exclusions and decision schedule for every programme. Remove an opportunity when a mandatory rule fails; time spent improving a strong-fit application is more valuable than trying to argue around an eligibility condition."}]],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],["$","section","3-Choose a path by degree before opening a form",{"className":"article-section","id":"section-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Choose a path by degree before opening a form"}],[["$","p","Undergraduate applicants may need early school nomination, as with the Pearson award. Master's candidates should decide whether the scholarship and admission are separate, as with Chevening, or handled through a course consortium, as with Erasmus Mundus. Doctoral applicants should identify research fit and any supervisor or partner-nomination requirement before drafting a proposal.",{"children":"Undergraduate applicants may need early school nomination, as with the Pearson award. Master's candidates should decide whether the scholarship and admission are separate, as with Chevening, or handled through a course consortium, as with Erasmus Mundus. Doctoral applicants should identify research fit and any supervisor or partner-nomination requirement before drafting a proposal."}],"$L1d"],"$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined","$L1e","$undefined","$undefined","$undefined"]}],"$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23"]}]
1d:["$","p","Choose your country, qualification and realistic budget first. Use the linked country guides for local eligibility details, then open the programme owner's current call before adding an award to your shortlist.",{"children":"Choose your country, qualification and realistic budget first. Use the linked country guides for local eligibility details, then open the programme owner's current call before adding an award to your shortlist."}]
